WEBVTT

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.650
Ryu! Ryu!

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:17.900
Kan... Everyone...

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.900
No questions.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.860
We don't know what's going on either.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:27.980
We were supposed to be summoned
by the Alchemist and reborn.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.400
So why?

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.070
I can't let you go to the library.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:36.400
I can't let you be reborn.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.900
What's that?

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:43.900
You will stay here within
this empty rift forever.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.610
Rift?

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:50.900
Is it him that's keeping us trapped here?

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.440
Hey, wait!

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:08.940
What's going on?

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:12.110
Why did it take the form of Akutagawa- <i>san</i> ?

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:14.190
Do you have any ideas?

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:16.690
No. Nothing I can say for sure.

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:19.820
But if I see him again, I may know.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:23.570
Our goal for now needs
to be getting out of here.

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:25.900
How would we do that, exactly?

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.110
I'm sorry. This is all my fault, I'm sure.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.610
What do you mean?

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:35.530
I need to tell you about him.

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:40.400
And why I made him.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:44.690
A fake, huh?

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:45.780
I'm...

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:51.730
Stop it! Get out of me!

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:53.400
Don't steal me away!

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:28.360
Episode 11

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.900
Gears

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.900
Ryunosuke 
Akutagawa

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:39.610
That's far enough, fake.

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:44.480
Well done, Hori- <i>kun</i> .

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:47.570
I'll protect Akutagawa- <i>san</i> 's books.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:49.280
Don't get in my way, please.

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:01.320
What's going on?

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.940
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ?

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:07.860
Would you give me that, Tatchanko?

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:11.400
You don't have the right to call me that!

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.480
Only Akutagawa- <i>san</i> does!

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:20.570
Stop it, Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.690
I told you, that's not who he is!

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:25.110
Give it up, fake!

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:31.150
Get our weapons too!

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:32.150
It's impossible!

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:35.030
You can't summon weapons inside the library!

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:37.280
Well, he's got one!

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:42.360
So this thing can even break
the laws of the Alchemist?

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:44.570
Ryu?

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:47.440
So it was you.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:50.690
Are you...

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.080
What is this?

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.150
The books...

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:15.190
Ryu!

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:22.780
Hey, Ryu! Come on, Ryu!

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:37.610
Stop it, please!

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.690
Don't get in my way!

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.820
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> , I...

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:46.980
I...!

00:05:56.650 --> 00:06:03.070
I won't let you hurt my friends...

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:06.110
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> , you're back to normal!

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:07.480
Move, Dazai.

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:10.980
I'm going to put him in confinement.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:20.320
What a strange state.

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:25.400
They've all been tainted,
but the Taint's progression is stopped.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.900
I've never seen this before.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:31.030
So we don't need to delve yet?

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.070
Yes.

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:36.690
With the progression of the Taint stopped,
the books will remain, for now.

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:38.530
What concerns us now is...

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:39.320
Kikuchi- <i>san</i> ?

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:40.860
How did it go?

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:43.110
He doesn't seem to be waking up.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:47.860
Whether it's progressing or not,
his book is tainted.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:50.860
It's put a heavy load on his psyche.

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:53.730
Damn that fake!

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:55.480
You don't need to say it like that!

00:06:55.480 --> 00:07:00.280
Don't tell me you still refuse
to admit he's a fake!

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:04.030
You saw his power! Admit it!

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:06.440
He's a Taint!

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:12.190
We need to talk about what happens to him next.

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:16.230
We know for sure that he's the one
that tainted Akutagawa's book.

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:18.320
So what do we do?

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:20.480
What else can we do?

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:23.610
He's a Taint. We deal with him.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:27.030
Wait a second. What do you mean, deal with him?

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:29.570
Taints are enemies to be defeated.

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:33.030
You've done that many times, haven't you?

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:36.360
Well... but...

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:38.530
Get over yourself, damn it!

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:40.860
Ryu's suffering right now!

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:43.980
And you saw who's at fault!

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:45.400
He's dangerous!

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.030
But he stopped!

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:48.940
He stopped!

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:51.530
We don't know if he'll
always be able to do that.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.150
Well, I'll stop him!

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:58.280
Can you say that to a comrade who's almost dead?

00:07:58.280 --> 00:07:59.860
Well...

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:01.360
Hold up.

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:03.820
Acting Director, I have a question.

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:05.190
What?

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:07.150
What is he like now?

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:09.780
Still a dangerous Taint?

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:12.570
No, he's calm right now.

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:15.860
He's the Akutagawa we know well.

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:18.480
Then the answer is obvious.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:20.860
There's no need to "deal with him."

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:26.190
Don't you think the fact that the Taint
progression has stopped means he's not an enemy?

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:27.690
What do you mean?

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:29.730
You're a dense little kid, aren't you?

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:31.320
I'm not a kid.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:35.940
He may be part Taint, yes.

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:40.280
But right now, he's the
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> we know.

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:45.780
The books aren't being Tainted because
he's doing his best to stop it, right?

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:47.820
Well...

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:50.360
You're a smooth talker.

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:54.150
You've moved the discussion
away from what matters.

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:58.610
Whether it's temporarily stopped
or not, he's still dangerous.

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:02.190
But that doesn't mean
you can just get rid of him!

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:04.480
Do you have another way, then?

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:06.530
I don't!

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:09.530
But I'm sure if we think, we can find out!

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:11.150
That's right.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:14.280
Some of the world's finest authors are here.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.530
If we all think, we can come up with something.

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:17.820
Let's do it, Dazai.

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:19.320
I'll help.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:20.860
So will we!

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:22.280
Guys...

00:09:22.280 --> 00:09:24.110
I don't get you, Dazai.

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:29.070
I thought you admired Ryunosuke Akutagawa.

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:33.730
Ryu's books are about to be destroyed,
and you're okay with that?

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:35.230
No!

00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:36.400
Then explain yourself!

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:43.480
You never met Ryu in life,
so you don't understand how we feel.

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:44.610
How you feel?

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:49.360
I couldn't save him!

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:54.860
If I'd been watching more closely,
Ryu wouldn't have killed himself!

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:57.940
It's not just your fault.

00:09:57.940 --> 00:10:02.400
I couldn't help him with his pain, either!

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:08.230
I always regretted that I couldn't save him!

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:14.280
And that's why we want to save Ryu now!

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:17.610
I'll protect his book, no matter what.

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:21.440
As a reader who loves them.

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:23.440
And as a friend.

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:25.940
We won't let Ryu's books be destroyed.

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:29.400
And we'll do whatever it takes to stop it!

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:36.070
Kan's right. Taints should be dealt with.

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:39.400
To protect Ryunosuke Akutagawa's books.

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:41.030
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ?

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:43.360
Don't call me by that name anymore, please.

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:46.610
What you see before you is just a Taint.

00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:51.820
We have to deal with him, then.

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:53.400
Do it, Kan.

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:57.440
You don't need to tell me...

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:10.690
They'll be getting rid of him tomorrow.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:18.280
If the Taint is destroyed, all of Ryunosuke
Akutagawa's books will be saved.

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:20.940
Everything will go back to normal.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:23.070
I talked to him once, here.

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:29.650
We don't know for sure that
the stars we see here are real.

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:35.780
They may all be fake, he said.

00:11:35.780 --> 00:11:37.860
I see.

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:40.820
But I think they're beautiful.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:43.480
To me, they seem to shine.

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:47.070
The reader's impressions are never wrong.

00:11:47.070 --> 00:11:52.730
When you read a book, you can
find it interesting or boring.

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:55.650
One is not superior to another.

00:11:55.650 --> 00:12:01.400
An individual's impressions of a work,
regardless of what they are, are correct.

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:04.980
You always say the most
complicated things, Shimazaki.

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:09.360
Do I? I thought I'd dumbed it down a lot.

00:12:11.690 --> 00:12:17.900
If you find fake stars beautiful,
your own impressions are correct.

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:24.190
And you're the only one who can decide
what to do based on that fact.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:38.230
As I said yesterday,
weapons cannot be used in the library.

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:43.320
So if we want to get rough,
we have to do it in a book, right?

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:46.070
And I've got the perfect one.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:50.650
Normally you can't go inside an untainted book.

00:12:50.650 --> 00:12:53.730
But if a Taint is with you...

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:58.980
...you can artificially create its tainted status.

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:02.780
We're lucky that I'm a Taint.

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:05.190
"Beyond the Pale of Vengeance"

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:05.190
Let's go.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:11.730
<i>Beyond the Pale of Vengeance</i> .

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:16.900
One of Kan's most famous works.

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:20.690
So this is the famous Blue Tunnel.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:23.110
It hasn't been named that yet.

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:27.610
The novel is the story of
the creation of the Blue Tunnel.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:33.230
The protagonist of this novel commits murder
and becomes a monk to atone.

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:36.730
He's doing a pilgrimage across
Japan when he stops here.

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:42.570
He learns that there are many
accidents here, and many have died.

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:47.780
So he decides to dig a tunnel
through the rock that will be safe.

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:50.900
To atone for his crimes...

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:55.570
He digs and digs for years.

00:13:55.570 --> 00:13:59.570
Some help, but they always go away in the end.

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:03.030
In the end, the man digs, alone.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:10.570
But then one day, the son of the man
he killed comes seeking vengeance.

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:22.070
Make it quick, please.

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:30.690
Any last words?

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:34.690
There's no need to ask
that question to a mere Taint.

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:39.690
Or is it you who isn't really ready for this?

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:42.030
Ryu was my best friend,

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:47.070
but I couldn't understand his pain.
I couldn't stop his suicide.

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:50.110
I always regretted that.

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:54.650
If I'd listened to him more,
made an effort to see him every day...

00:14:54.650 --> 00:15:01.070
I kept thinking of possibilities
and blaming myself for not doing them.

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:05.530
I wanted to save him.

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:07.320
But...

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:10.320
Now I'm trying to kill him.

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:13.730
He's a Taint. Not the real Ryu.

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:18.320
I know that, but you still look like Ryu to me.

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:21.480
Of course I'm not going to like it.

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:23.480
I see.

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:28.190
But it's the only way to save Ryu's books.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:29.690
So I...

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:54.110
Dazai- <i>kun</i> ?

00:15:54.110 --> 00:15:55.730
What are you doing?

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:57.780
I won't let you kill him!

00:15:57.780 --> 00:15:59.030
What?

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:01.570
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> is one of us!

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:03.150
I won't let you kill him!

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:05.610
Have you gone mad? He's...

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:07.730
So what if he's a fake?

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:11.110
He's the one who saved me!

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:14.190
He saved many others, too!

00:16:14.190 --> 00:16:17.150
He may not be Ryunosuke Akutagawa!

00:16:17.150 --> 00:16:19.440
He may be a Taint!

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:21.440
But still...

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:23.150
Fake or not...

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:26.940
...he's one of us!

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:28.320
Dazai- <i>kun</i> .

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:30.780
I see.

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:33.230
Looks like you won't be persuaded, then.

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:48.690
Stop it!

00:17:00.650 --> 00:17:04.440
Do you know what you're doing?

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:06.730
We sure do!

00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:10.150
I love Akutagawa- <i>san</i> !

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:14.730
I can't let his books disappear!

00:17:14.730 --> 00:17:16.530
So I'll protect him!

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:18.780
And if you get in my way...

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:20.570
...prepare to suffer!

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:23.570
I'm disappointed.

00:17:23.570 --> 00:17:26.900
I can't believe you'd side with a Taint!

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:27.940
Shut up.

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:30.650
We're not siding with a Taint.

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:34.820
We just don't like the way you're doing things!

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:41.780
You're too emotional.

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:45.230
Can't you take a more objective view?

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:01.610
What's wrong with letting
your emotions drive you?

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:05.440
Let your emotions determine how you live.
Let them determine the motion of your pen.

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:08.070
That's how the Reprobates work.

00:18:19.190 --> 00:18:23.690
I misunderstood the man named Osamu Dazai.

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:25.570
I thought he was unserious and selfish,

00:18:25.570 --> 00:18:30.280
but cared deeply about literature.

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:33.190
I never thought he'd help destroy a book.

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:36.190
Especially not Ryu's books!

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:37.570
No!

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:41.780
I don't want his books destroyed!

00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:44.940
But there's a way to defend
his books without doing this!

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:46.530
I'll find it!

00:18:56.400 --> 00:19:02.110
I want to protect Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> 's
books, and him too!

00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:03.860
You...

00:19:03.860 --> 00:19:06.730
Don't worry, Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> .

00:19:06.730 --> 00:19:08.860
I'll save you.

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:13.320
Just like you've saved everyone...

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:18.440
You would still call me Akutagawa?

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:22.530
You're such a fool...

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:34.900
Stop it! Stay inside me!

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:36.690
Why do you resist?

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:38.860
Who are you?

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:41.110
You still can't remember?

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:43.070
Remember what?

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:45.730
Why you're here.

00:19:45.730 --> 00:19:48.730
Why you were born.

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:50.440
Born?

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:53.610
Remember the meaning of your birth.

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:55.940
The meaning of your war.

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:04.780
Ryunosuke Akutagawa, my pen name,

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:09.150
at some point seemed to become
its own distinct human being.

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:14.520
"Rashomon"

00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:15.070
The time when I was happy my books were selling
well had long since passed.

00:20:15.070 --> 00:20:19.070
Now there was nothing left but pain.

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:23.570
Everyone wanted me to write the next story.

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:26.980
A thrilling book like my last one.

00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:29.940
It was like they were threatening me.

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:36.320
But I'd lost interest in my own books.

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:38.730
<i>Portrait of Hell</i> . <i>Rashomon</i> .

00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:41.320
They were loved, yes.

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:45.440
But neither were the story
I really wanted to write.

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:45.550
Naoya Shiga

